      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The heat of the steam is a warm hug, but it feels like a gentle caress from a giant, sleepy goblin who hasn't learned to fight yet. Inside my thick, armored coat, I am not dying; I am simply going to sleep, and I have a very specific, very stubborn plan to wake up later.\n\nAs the temperature drops, that gentle goblin wakes up, stretches, and says, \"Hey, it's time to eat.\" I don't just sit there; I actively *wait* for the food to cool, like a little goblin hiding in a cave until the sun goes down. I am a tiny, invisible goblin in a pot of soup, and I am perfectly happy to be ignored.\n\nWhen the temperature finally falls below my threshold, I burst open with a loud, explosive pop, like a goblin popping a bubble with a stick. I am ready to feast on the protein, and I am not going to stop until I have eaten everything in sight.\n\nSo, remember: if the food gets too hot, I go to sleep. If the food gets too cold, I wake up and start eating. I am a goblin in a pot, and I am waiting for",
      "source": "target",
